      "writtenOn": "2020-09-03T22:02:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: I\u0027m assuming that more board versions are expected, which is why I suggested an\nif (version \u003d\u003d 0) {...}\nelse if (version \u003d\u003d 1) {...} etc. formulation earlier. That way, you could just add an else if clause when you add support for a new board version later.\n\nThe way this is written currently, setting stuff for board version 0 and doing nothing for other values, you\u0027ll have to change the structure when you add board version 1. It\u0027s up to you.",
      "revId": "51b9f32d1307d83b03146a09004f9c1cf9298268",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
